<overview>
<p>A flatbed railcar (or flatcar) is a type of open-deck freight car designed without sides, roofs, or ends, featuring a simple, flat platform for carrying large, heavy, or irregularly shaped cargo. They are essentially flat, versatile platforms used for transporting goods that do not require protection from the weather.</p>
</overview>

